From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P80 builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Teclast P80: deep Doze without a motion sensor

DeviceIdleController.scheduleAlarmLocked() returns early while
config_autoPowerModeUseMotionSensor is true and there is no
significant-motion sensor, so the P80 (accelerometer only) never left
light idle: 96 % light idle and no deep idle in 2-hour standby tests on
LineageOS 23.2 and 24.0. Turn the motion requirement off, as the
framework does for devices whose movement should not count.
---
diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -54,6 +54,13 @@
     <bool name="config_isDesktopModeSupported">false</bool>
     <bool name="config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops">false</bool>
 
+    <!-- Teclast P80: deep Doze. DeviceIdleController only schedules the deep idle steps when
+         config_autoPowerModeUseMotionSensor is false or a significant-motion sensor exists; the
+         P80 has only an accelerometer, so it stayed in light idle while asleep (96 % of a
+         2-hour standby test). Without motion detection deep idle follows the screen-off and
+         stationary timeouts alone, as on TVs. -->
+    <bool name="config_autoPowerModeUseMotionSensor">false</bool>
+
     <bool name="config_supportAudioSourceUnprocessed">true</bool>
 
     <string-array name="config_packagesExemptFromSuspension" translatable="false">
-- 
2.43.0
